{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>All the nations, etc.</b> Now perhaps someone will say that Israel did not know these future things, for they are blind — perhaps among the nations and their sages there is one who did know. Who among you will declare these future things, and let them make us hear former things that have passed, which they declared before they came to be:" "<b>Let them give their witnesses.</b> Whoever heard this:" "<b>[and they shall be justified].</b> Then they will be righteous of mouth:" "<b>Let them hear.</b> The witnesses, likewise:" "<b>and say: Truth.</b> So it was:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:43.533189418Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}